{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/733659-ex3-eclipse-caste-and-non-solar-charms","id":733659,"title":"[EX3] Eclipse caste and non-Solar charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-27T19:00:14-07:00","id":733659,"title":"[EX3] Eclipse caste and non-Solar charms","content":"A fellow player in a game that we've roughshod converted to 3E at this point brought up an interesting question, partially on account of not being a hardcore Exalted player.<br /> <br /> The Eclipse Caste power that allows them to learn non-Solar charms doesn't seem to actually specify if they require a teacher this time around. My immediate assumption was they did, but upon giving it a bit more thought, it occurred to me that part of the point of the &quot;Eclipse&quot; Keyword going forward might be to circumvent the prior edition's need for teachers. Makes it much easier to learn oddball charms, but still isn't overwhelmingly crazy because it's only a very specific handful of charms.<br /> <br /> Any of the devs care to weigh in on this, or did I miss something somewhere in my reading?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatar